keywords:
  - emergent spacetime
  - spectral dimension
  - network theory
  - varying speed of light
  - quantum gravity
  - cosmology
abstract: >
  DRND outlines a background-independent framework in which spacetime, matter degrees
  of freedom, and effective dynamical laws emerge from an evolving discrete graph of causal
  relations. The spectral dimension is treated as a dynamical, environment-dependent observable,
  motivating a toy phenomenology where topology-dependent propagation can bias cosmological
  distance inference.